UPDATE 2026-09-06 (seat06): PRIOR MARKER TEXT WAS STALE IN THE DANGEROUS DIRECTION -- the 2026-09-05
symptom description ("SCRIP exits rc=1 printing exactly one line, `no /etc/passwd`") no longer reproduces
on the current build (RT_TAG f65f143e2f): the `open("/etc/passwd")` list-literal construct it described
now runs to completion, and the program instead dies LATER with `ERROR 022 -- Undefined function called`.
Re-bisecting the full file surfaced TWO unrelated, now fully root-caused defects (same "one confusing
combined shape, two independent mechanisms" pattern this row hit earlier on `errkwds`), both rowed to
hq_B, plus a third still-open item this session did not chase:

(1) `L := sort(L)` on a list containing `&input`/`&output`/`&errout`/two open() file values silently
    no-ops -- SCRIP's sort() leaves the list in its ORIGINAL construction order instead of icont's
    image()-string order. Root cause: sort's default comparator returns "" for any non-string/non-integer
    element (src/runtime/by_name_dispatch.c:4257-4267), so every pair compares equal and nothing ever
    swaps. Rowed as `icon-sort-default-comparator-returns-empty-key-for-files-and-other-opaque-types-so-
    they-never-reorder` (rank 2, hq_B), DONE-WHEN written and exercised red before trusting.

(2) The `\` (limitation) operator lets exactly ONE EXTRA result through for any N (E \ N yields N+1, not
    N) -- confirmed at N=1 and N=4. Root cause: src/lower/lower_icon.c:813-825 (case TT_LIMIT) wires the
    box so the wrapped expression's first evaluation runs before the box's own count-check is ever
    reached, so the check only ever constrains the 2nd/3rd/... invocation onward. This ONE mechanism
    explains both of io.icn's own limitation-operator lines once traced with the real stdin sidecar:
    `every write(!&input \ 2)` silently consumes one extra input line (the ungated call's read happens,
    its value just never reaches write); `every write(!&input) \ 2` prints one extra line (the ungated
    call's write() side effect fires before any check exists for that round). Rowed as
    `icon-limitation-operator-lets-exactly-one-extra-result-through-for-any-n` (rank 2, hq_B), DONE-WHEN
    written and exercised red before trusting.

(3) UPDATE 2026-09-06 (seat06, second pass -- item (3) above is now root-caused, not a guess): the ERROR
    022 abort is `flush()` -- confirmed with a standalone 4-line witness (`open("/etc/passwd")` then
    `write(image(flush(m)))` aborts identically). NOT the args()/`_bt[]` arity-table family guessed above
    (that family returns WRONG counts, it does not abort) -- checked and ruled out. Same shape as the
    already-rowed icon-serial-builtin-is-entirely-unimplemented and
    icon-errorclear-builtin-is-entirely-unimplemented-and-aborts-the-program: `flush` is listed in the
    arity-metadata tables (src/runtime/by_name_dispatch.c:3908, :4709) but there is no `BID_flush` enum
    value anywhere in the codebase (confirmed: zero grep hits), so there is no dispatch arm and every call
    falls straight to the undefined-user-function abort path. This is the true current blocker stopping
    `io.icn` before ~115 remaining lines of its output can even be attempted. Rowed as
    `icon-flush-builtin-is-entirely-unimplemented-and-aborts-the-program` (rank 1, hq_B), DONE-WHEN
    written and exercised red before trusting.

